----ENDF/B-VII        MATERIAL 3800                               3800 1451    7
-----ATOMIC RELAXATION DATA                                       3800 1451    8
------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               3800 1451    9
==================================================================3800 1451   10
The Livermore Evaluated Atomic Data Library (EADL) in the         3800 1451   11
ENDF-6 Format. Translated from the Livermore ENDL format          3800 1451   12
to the ENDF-6 Format by Bob MacFarlane (Los Alamos).              3800 1451   13
==================================================================3800 1451   14
  Contents                                                        3800 1451   15
==================================================================3800 1451   16
  MF/MT    Description                                            3800 1451   17
==================================================================3800 1451   18
  28/533   Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons       3800 1451   19
==================================================================3800 1451   20
  Warning                                                         3800 1451   21
==================================================================3800 1451   22
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 3800 1451   23
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist3800 1451   24
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  3800 1451   25
==================================================================3800 1451   26
  Definition of Data                                              3800 1451   27
==================================================================3800 1451   28
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                3800 1451   29
==================================================================3800 1451   30
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 3800 1451   31
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       3800 1451   32
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 3800 1451   33
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              3800 1451   34
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   3800 1451   35
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     3800 1451   36
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            3800 1451   37
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  3800 1451   38
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     3800 1451   39
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     3800 1451   40
   calculates these spectra.                                      3800 1451   41
==================================================================3800 1451   42
  References                                                      3800 1451   43
==================================================================3800 1451   44
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 3800 1451   45
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   3800 1451   46
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 3800 1451   47
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 3800 1451   48
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 3800 1451   49
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    3800 1451   50
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        3800 1451   51
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    3800 1451   52
                                                                  3800 1451   53
  These are the primary references to the contents of this library3800 1451   54
  and they contain a complete list of references to the sources   3800 1451   55
  of data used in this library, methods of evaluation, accuracy   3800 1451   56
  of the data, etc.                                               3800 1451   57
==================================================================3800 1451   58
  History                                                         3800 1451   59
==================================================================3800 1451   60
 (1) November, 1991 - Initial release in the ENDL format.         3800 1451   61
 (2) October,  2001 - Initial release in the ENDF-6 format.       3800 1451   62
